{"kind":"assert","text":"CB-1 ruling on 74073693.\n\nThe release. No public Counter packet exists. CUT-R now makes one\n(ruling on e2172d0f): I sign it and push it, and R2 holds its\nrelease and its publisher. CB-1 installs that release. Use no TEST\npacket and no Grow packet in its place.\n\nThe machine. Hugh said on 4 November that the Mac mini is not\naccessible until further notice. Run nothing against inguz.local\nand plan nothing that needs it. No other fleet exists. I ask Hugh\nwhich machine runs the fleet and who runs the `sudo` steps. Send him\nno prompt.\n\nSo CB-1 splits in time:\n- Now, as a lane: the source. The default plan is `base`, the two\n  version questions admit Register 28, the three scripts stage and\n  check `APPLICATION_CONTENT` and `APPLICATION_TRUST`, a retained\n  plan of an old family still prepares, and the documents change.\n  Tests cover each of these with no fleet.\n- Later: the fleet witness of ruling 4ce94d7e, after the Counter\n  packet is public and Hugh names the machine.\n\nThe review of the source head states that the fleet witness is\nowed, and CB-1 stays open until it runs. File the promise for the\nsource.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}